# INDAI Service Page — Copy Template (Canonical)

## Status
FINAL / LOCKED

## Purpose
This document defines the canonical copy structure for all INDAI service pages.
It ensures consistency in positioning, tone, and logic across all services.
Used as a single source of truth for content, design, and implementation.

---

## Service Page — Canonical Copy Structure

### 1. Service Hero

#### H1 (Service Name)
[Service name in neutral, technical wording]

#### Intro (2–3 lines)
A concise explanation of what the service is, when it is applied, and what task it solves.
No marketing exaggeration. No promises beyond technical scope.

---

### 2. What This Service Is

A clear description of:
- the nature of the work,
- the type of intervention,
- the technical purpose of the service.

Focus on **what is done**, not why it is “better than others”.

---

### 3. Applicable Objects

List of objects and environments where the service can be applied.
Examples:
- equipment,
- structures,
- components,
- industrial or non-industrial objects.

No restriction to “production enterprises” unless technically required.

---

### 4. Technologies & Methods

Description of:
- applied technologies,
- pressure ranges,
- materials,
- methods (hydrodynamic, cryogenic, cutting, etc.).

Only factual, verifiable information.

---

### 5. Safety & Compliance

Description of:
- safety principles,
- compliance with regulations,
- HSE considerations,
- operational control.

No claims of “absolute safety”.

---

### 6. Expected Result

Neutral description of the technical result of the service.
Examples:
- surface condition after treatment,
- removal of specific contaminants,
- readiness for further operations.

No universal claims like “increase productivity” unless strictly applicable.

---

### 7. How We Work

Brief outline of the working approach:
- assessment,
- method selection,
- execution,
- control.

Aligned with the general INDAI workflow.

---

### 8. Entry to Dialogue

Soft invitation to interaction:
- ask a technical question,
- discuss an object,
- upload photos or documentation.

No aggressive CTA.
